  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It took me a while to figure out what was going on with that thing.\n-0. Upon opening this beta, I was very confused as I opened my main menu, and it was just randomly following my view fluidly wherever I looked, hiding my laser pointer cursor, preventing me from clicking on it at all, and preventing me from letting it go. This was my initial impression - whatever was going on wasn't intuitive at all.\nI think the fixes are simple, as seen in the following points:\n-1. The [   +   ] move bar seems to be present when it shouldn't. Even with the menu closed, nothing open at all, its \"ghost\" keeps flashing in and out when I move around, presumably when my hand flashes over it.\n-2. Clicking on (grabbing) that bar removes the laser pointer on all other menus, which is confusing, especially when the main menu isn't even open. This should stop being a problem once the bar only shows if the menu is open.\n-3. I didn't know that bar even existed until I saw its ghost flashing a few times and realized what it was and what it was tied to.\nThe problem here is that even when I had my main menu open, I didn't know it was there, because it's completely invisible until you hover over it.\nI think it should start partially transparent and become fully opaque when you mouse over it.\n-4. That bar needs to be disabled at all other times (when the main menu is not open). It's pretty much omnipresent. It's just getting in the way.\n-5. Playspace mover is a little funny with horizon adjust, but that's not your problem, and not a reason not to have this great QoL update.\n-6. I love everything else about this update. This is absolutely great. This affects things that benefit 100% of every user for 100% of their playtime. It's so comfortable to use while laying down (for the not-prone-to-motionsickness like me).\nThe horizon adjust + menu positioning makes VRChat easier to use than Steam's default VR overlay and I hope Steam follows in your footsteps.\nI dunno why you guys never thought to do stuff like this ages ago, but I'm not salty about it either :)",
